simone bile's decision is intensifying a  new conversation about  mental health and sports especially on  the world stage  three-time olympic gymnast dominique  dawes knows what it's like to be  in the spotlight she helped the u.s win  its first gold medal  in the women's gymnastics team final  back in 1996.  the team of seven earned the nickname  the magnificent seven  dominique dawes joins us now good  morning so good to see you  and you know you had to face your own  obstacles  at that time you're the first  african-american individual medal winner  in artistic gymnastics  you have to in some ways i'm guessing  relate to what simone biles is going  through were you shocked  by this news that she pulled out of  these events so far  i can certainly relate wholeheartedly i  remember stepping out into the georgia  dome before the 1996 olympic games  and prior to doing that having an  emotional breakdown just feeling  all the pressure that uh team usa felt  from needing to make history so  when i awoke the other day to hear that  simone biles had pulled out of the  competition i did not think it was for  mental issues i thought it was possibly  because of an injury  then when i heard it was a decision that  she made after going through a certain  vault and having a mental block i could  again relate to that because i went  through a lot of mental blocks  i commended her for listening to her  inner voice  and doing what was best for simone biles  gymnasts are usually in a very  controlled environment we are trained to  be robots we don't listen to our inner  voice it's been muted  and i love the fact that she listened to  herself and she did what was best for  her mental health  as well as to ward off any possible  injury i know dominique what did you  think when you heard her say the other  day she feel  she felt the whole weight of the world  on her shoulders  my heart just went out to her knowing  that she was feeling  such tremendous pressure yes the sport  of gymnastics is filled with a great  deal of anxiety a great deal of fear a  great deal of intimidation  and a great deal of pressure and for her  being known as the goat the greatest of  all time  having a goat on your lead guitar doing  an interview with the goat i was like  that's a little much and very ballsy  however  i felt as if you know what she can  overcome whatever pressure there is but  she's human she's going to feel she's  going to hurt she's going to be wounded  and now as a mother of four and now even  standing in my own gymnastics gym here  in maryland  so dominique dawes gymnastics academy  it's all about creating a very healthy  and encouraging environment one in which  that's not filled with pressure  boy dominique the mother of four just  think about let us take that in for a  second standing in your own  gymnasium go you do you think the the  the effect of not having family and  friends in the stands  what role that must play because i would  think that that's she said it's the  first time that she's ever done it  without them and she's used to looking  at  looking up at them yes her support  system is so important it's important  for everyone  i love the fact that she leans on her  catholic faith but her mom and dad are  also so very important and her sister  and as you can see online  she actually has a boyfriend she has  friends the young girls on this team  they actually seem like they get along  and they support one another you need  that  atmosphere of your family and your  friends and your fans right there in the  in the stands there cheering you on they  add to the pressure i will say that  however that's something that is a  comfort if you're used to seeing them  there  dominique we also saw naomi osaka  withdraw from some tennis events  recently do you think this is uh this is  a turning point for athletes in  in looking after their mental health  more and being vocal about it i  really think this is from the dialogue  that was created from the metoo movement  and then when everything came out in  2016 with regards to the scandal of  larry nassar the olympic team doctor  who sexually abused hundreds of young  women now we're speaking about the  unhealthy culture in the sport of  gymnastics  now we're talking about the importance  of mental health as you guys mentioned  earlier michael phelps's  piece on hbo talking about his  depression things of that nature this is  a wonderful platform for athletes to now  express what they've been experiencing  with regards to anxiety with regards to  depression with regards to pressure and  i love that these athletes are listening  to their inner voice and doing what's  best for them  and dominique to that point about larry  nassar how much of an impact do you  think  that plays on simone bile's psyche  because this was an  organization that she felt didn't do  enough and here she is  on that stage for that organization that  she feels didn't protect her and other  athletes  yes i admire simone biles more for her  speaking out and speaking her truth than  her amazing athletic prounish what she  does out there  i am so thankful i'm retired she is  generations above her competition  but the fact that she's on the floor and  she's even said this as the only  survivor competing on the floor  she felt as if usa gymnastics would  brush all the unhealthy aspects of this  culture under the rug  if she were not out there the fact that  she said that and she was still  competing under usa  gymnastics that to me was quite  courageous  and the fact that she had to endure that  um shows how strong she is  yeah she's been courageous in so many  ways dominique dawes thank you so much  for being with us this morning
 

